; cortex size. The head's ONE source (cortex.loon) takes its shell size from here, so one file drives every size:
;   mini (this file, default): 3.5" face, 164 x 104 x 121 overall
;   full (size-full.loon):     7" face, the shell plan x 1.4, same dock
; Selection is by file: export.sh (and any importer) copies the size it wants in as `size.loon` next to
; cortex.loon (module resolution: a file next to the importer wins over the lib path).
; These are the ONLY size inputs cortex.loon reads: the four shell planes and the 7-inch display's envelope.
; Everything else in cortex.loon either derives from these or is a datasheet part size, which does not scale.
[pub let size-mini true]
[pub let size-full false]

[pub let hh [if size-full 169.0 120.6]]            ; height
[pub let hw [if size-full 114.5 81.8]]             ; half width
[pub let x-face [if size-full 64.4 46.0]]          ; the flat face plane
[pub let x-back [if size-full -81.2 -58.0]]        ; the flat back plane (reaches past the neck: no craning)

; the full's face: Waveshare 7inch HDMI LCD (C), 164.9 x 107 x 8 outline, active 154.21 x 85.92 (wiki Dimension /
; Display Area). Its own bezel is the dead front, like the mini's 4-inch variant: the tub gets a window with a
; 5 mm bond land, the display sits 1 mm proud. The mini ignores these.
[pub let d7-w 166.0]                               ; the display's outline + 1 mm margin each side
[pub let d7-h 108.0]
[pub let d7-t 8.0]                                 ; outline to the connector backs (wiki Dimension)
[pub let d7-act-w 154.21]
[pub let d7-act-h 85.92]
